00:30:35.054 --> 00:30:37.370
[MACHINE WHISTLING]

00:30:37.370 --> 00:30:39.710
Well, OK, Mark, "I want
to push a Docker image

00:30:39.710 --> 00:30:42.480
to Google Container
Registry via Docker push.

00:30:42.480 --> 00:30:45.800
So how can I do that so I don't
have to use gcloud Docker --

00:30:45.800 --> 00:30:47.060
push every time?"

00:30:47.060 --> 00:30:48.590
MARK MANDEL: Well, that's an
excellent question, Mandy.

00:30:48.590 --> 00:30:49.040
[HONK]

00:30:49.040 --> 00:30:49.539
Mandy.

00:30:49.539 --> 00:30:50.540
[MELANIE LAUGHS]

00:30:50.540 --> 00:30:51.610
MELANIE WARRICK: That's
right, I'm Mandy.

00:30:51.610 --> 00:30:52.220
MARK MANDEL: You're Mandy.

00:30:52.220 --> 00:30:53.930
Well, that's an excellent
question, Melanie.

00:30:53.930 --> 00:30:55.554
I'm so glad that you
asked the question

00:30:55.554 --> 00:30:56.649
that I asked you to ask.

00:30:56.649 --> 00:30:58.190
MELANIE WARRICK:
It's very convenient

00:30:58.190 --> 00:30:59.040
how we worked that out.

00:30:59.040 --> 00:30:59.940
MARK MANDEL: Yeah, exactly.

00:30:59.940 --> 00:31:02.231
So I wanted to talk about
this for a couple of reasons.

00:31:02.231 --> 00:31:05.150
One of which is, sometimes
it's just easier or more

00:31:05.150 --> 00:31:07.280
ideal to simply say,
hey, Docker push,

00:31:07.280 --> 00:31:09.530
rather than using the gcloud
command to do some stuff,

00:31:09.530 --> 00:31:11.580
maybe CI pipelines,
that kind of stuff.

00:31:11.580 --> 00:31:14.210
But the other side of
this is actually also

00:31:14.210 --> 00:31:16.972
some things around
deprecation, as well.

00:31:16.972 --> 00:31:18.180
We'll start at the top level.

00:31:18.180 --> 00:31:20.720
So if you want to
simply be able to say,

00:31:20.720 --> 00:31:23.150
Docker push or Docker pull
from a Container Registry using

00:31:23.150 --> 00:31:24.705
your gcloud
authentication, there's

00:31:24.705 --> 00:31:27.391
a command you can run called
gcloud auth configure-docker

00:31:27.391 --> 00:31:29.640
And what that will do is
that'll set up some handlers,

00:31:29.640 --> 00:31:32.292
add some credential helpers
within your Docker credentials,

00:31:32.292 --> 00:31:34.250
and set things up basically
so it's essentially

00:31:34.250 --> 00:31:35.240
a seamless process.

00:31:35.240 --> 00:31:36.740
This is the preferred way.

00:31:36.740 --> 00:31:38.210
We strongly recommend
that you use

00:31:38.210 --> 00:31:39.680
this method whenever possible.

00:31:39.680 --> 00:31:41.810
It provides secure
short-lived access

00:31:41.810 --> 00:31:44.600
to your project resources--
if a read the documentation.

00:31:44.600 --> 00:31:46.130
And so basically
that is the way.

00:31:46.130 --> 00:31:47.713
So if you ever find
that you're having

00:31:47.713 --> 00:31:49.970
issues with, say, gcloud
Docker for any reason,

00:31:49.970 --> 00:31:50.740
use this instead.

00:31:50.740 --> 00:31:52.190
It's definitely much better.

00:31:52.190 --> 00:31:54.740
But it's worth noting
then, for this very reason,

00:31:54.740 --> 00:31:56.840
that gcloud Docker is
currently only recommended

00:31:56.840 --> 00:31:59.480
for Docker client versions
older than 1.13, which

00:31:59.480 --> 00:32:02.000
don't support the use
of credential helpers

00:32:02.000 --> 00:32:03.170
or anything like that.

00:32:03.170 --> 00:32:07.037
So it's worth noting that
I've seen people try and use

00:32:07.037 --> 00:32:08.870
gcloud Docker with newer
versions of Docker,

00:32:08.870 --> 00:32:10.760
and sometimes it didn't work
and people get confused,

00:32:10.760 --> 00:32:11.880
and that kind of stuff.

00:32:11.880 --> 00:32:13.760
So if you're on a new
version of Docker use

00:32:13.760 --> 00:32:16.500
the credential helpers
gcloud auth configure-docker,

00:32:16.500 --> 00:32:18.830
and that'll make your
lives all that easier.

00:32:18.830 --> 00:32:20.650
